# Loaded instead of .env when APP_ENV=testing (phpunit.xml sets it): Laravel prefers ".env.<APP_ENV>"
# over ".env" when that file exists. It is deliberately empty. Its only job is to exist, so that the
# developer's real .env (credentials, mail, S3, APP_URL...) never leaks into the test suite and a
# test run does not depend on what happens to be configured on the machine.
#
# Everything the tests need is set in phpunit.xml. Do not put values here, and never put secrets.
